cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use ADC Peptide Mapper in your research, please cite it using
  the metadata below. Replace the doi placeholder with your real Zenodo
  DOI after uploading the release (see User Manual Section 11 for instructions).

title: "ADC Peptide Mapper"
version: "0.8"
date-released: "2026-06-13"
abstract: >
  An R Shiny application for in-silico proteolytic digestion of
  Antibody-Drug Conjugate (ADC) sequences, uniqueness checking against
  pre-built Human, Cynomolgus Monkey, and Rat proteome backgrounds
  (UniProt Swiss-Prot reviewed + TrEMBL), and instrument-specific
  transition list generation for LC-MS/MS MRM and high-resolution method
  development.

  Version 0.8 adds: Drug-to-Antibody Ratio (DAR) distribution modeling
  (DAR0 – DARn) with full MRM transition list generation per DAR level;
  site-specific conjugation chemistry classification (cysteine thiol-
  maleimide, lysine NHS-ester / hydrazone, site-specific); linker
  biotransformation variable modifications (maleimide ring hydrolysis,
  succinimide ring-opening, thioether oxidation to sulfoxide, disulfide
  loss, conjugation-site deamidation); averagine-based isotope envelope
  calculation (Senko 1995); target-decoy FDR estimation (Käll 2008);
  cross-species uniqueness filtering (Human / Cyno / Rat co-species
  analysis); cRAP contaminant database integration; MS Amanda 3.0 and
  Crux/Tide search engine support; a self-contained unit test suite
  (79 tests, 100% pass rate); and sub-mDa mass accuracy benchmarking
  against IgG1 tryptic peptide reference standards.
type: software
license: MIT

authors:
  - family-names: Wase
    given-names: Nishikant
    email: nishikant.wase@gmail.com

keywords:
  - antibody-drug conjugate
  - ADC
  - proteomics
  - tryptic digest
  - multi-enzyme digest
  - peptide mapping
  - transition list
  - drug-to-antibody ratio
  - DAR modeling
  - site-specific conjugation
  - linker biotransformation
  - cysteine conjugation
  - lysine conjugation
  - Skyline
  - MRM
  - R Shiny
  - mass spectrometry
  - heavy labelling
  - stable isotope labelling
  - SILAC
  - drug-linker payload
  - ADCDB
  - collision energy
  - Thermo
  - SCIEX
  - Bruker
  - Agilent
  - Waters
  - isotope distribution
  - averagine
  - target-decoy FDR
  - MS Amanda
  - Crux

# ── Replace the placeholder below with your real Zenodo DOI ──────────────
# Steps:
#   1. Go to https://zenodo.org/deposit/new
#   2. Upload ADC_Peptide_Mapper_v0.8.zip (Upload type = Software)
#   3. Fill in title, author, version, description and click Publish
#   4. Zenodo assigns a permanent DOI (e.g. 10.5281/zenodo.NNNNNNN)
#   5. Replace XXXXXXX below with your real record number
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20681412"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20681412"

